  "notes": [
    "Irregular -IR verb with an *e→i* stem change (same pattern as *pedir*, *servir*, *repetir*): the stressed *e* becomes *i* everywhere except Pretérito Imperfecto, Futuro Simple, and Condicional, which stay fully regular",
    "Unlike *e→ie* and *o→ue* verbs, this stem change also appears in the Pretérito Indefinido 3rd-person forms (*midió, midieron* — not \"medió, medieron\") and carries through to nosotros in Subjuntivo Presente (*midamos*, not \"medamos\") and Imperfecto de Subjuntivo (*midiéramos*)",
    "Past participle: *medido* (regular)",
    "Means \"to measure\" — *mide la habitación antes de comprar los muebles* (measure the room before buying the furniture); also used reflexively/figuratively for height: *mide 1.80 metros* (he/she is 1.80 meters tall)",
    "Related: *medida* (measurement, measure — *tomar medidas* = to take measures/measurements), *medidor* (meter, gauge)"
  ],
